# WS5-06 (ports, messages, signals). Sources: spec/appendix-stdlib.md §13.2 and the exec
# autodocs (CreatePort/CreateMsgPort allocate a signal bit and DeletePort frees it;
# PutMsg/GetMsg/ReplyMsg; a message must be replied or freed). Expected: payload 41 + 1
# and nothing left allocated.
# Detector: probe.py --vamos-leaks fails an Amiga run whose vamos log reports a
# library or device left open ("can't expunge … open count") or orphan AllocMem
# memory (shown to fire on the seeded program 500-seeded-leak.c in the red check).
profiles: hosted-amiga-13 hosted-amiga
expect: output
contrast: createMessage(borrow r, 41) ==> createMessage(borrow r, 50)
contrast-expect: output
--- output
42
--- contrast-output
51
